#
# The HRX toolchain the build compiles with (docs/hrx.md, "The toolchain"; docs/releases.md,
# "What is in a release"): TheRock's ROCm SDK at one nightly version, for one GPU target, fetched
# by scripts/fetch-rocm-sdk.sh into third_party/toolchain/rocm-sdk-<version>-<gfx>. It is pinned
# like every other upstream (hrx-system, llama.cpp, the kernel and runtime pins) so that a fresh
# box needs only this repository: nothing outside it, and no HIP_DEVICE_LIB_PATH / ROCM_PATH /
# HIP_PATH, is required to build. cmake/hrx.cmake defaults to the fetched
# copy; /opt/rocm-therock stays an override (ROCM_PATH or -DONEBIT_HRX_TOOLCHAIN=<dir>).
#
# Move the pin by hand, after the HRX checks on Strix Halo (docs/hrx.md, "Checking HRX"). The
# version is a nightly wheel version from the index below, and the gfx target is what
# --offload-arch builds; it is the same target the box has.
version=10.3.0a20261031
gfx=gfx1151
index=https://nightly.repo.amd.com/rocm/whl-next/
require=bin/amdclang bin/hipcc bin/hipconfig
